## Development

```bash
# Build
go build -o {{.BinaryName}} {{.MainPackage}}

# Run locally (with epack SDK)
epack sdk run ./{{.BinaryName}}

# Watch mode: auto-rebuild on file changes
epack sdk run --watch .

# Run conformance tests (builds the project first)
epack sdk test .
```
{{- if eq .Kind "collector"}}

`make conformance`, which CI runs, passes `testdata/conformance.json` and a
`--secret` for each variable listed in the Makefile's `CONFORMANCE_SECRETS`.
Keep the config free of secrets. Each `--secret` variable gets a canary value:
conformance fails if any output prints it and checks that the rejected
credential exits 3. To run the output checks against a real collection, run
`epack sdk test .` with real credentials in the environment.
{{- end}}

### Manual Testing

```bash
# Test capabilities
./{{.BinaryName}} --capabilities

# Run conformance at the epack version go.mod pins, as CI does
go install -tags conformance github.com/locktivity/epack/cmd/epack-conformance@"$(go list -m -f '{{"{{"}}.Version{{"}}"}}' github.com/locktivity/epack)"
$(go env GOPATH)/bin/epack-conformance {{.Kind}} ./{{.BinaryName}}{{if eq .Kind "collector"}} --config testdata/conformance.json{{end}}
```

